  "query_preview": "..For the remainder of today and tonight...Expect fair\nand dry weather with generally light winds and seasonable \ntemperatures under dry southwest flow aloft.\n\nOn Saturday and Sunday...A weak low pressure system will make its\nway across Arizona. Look for generally light winds with\ntemperatures fairly typical for this time of year. The low will\nbring with it some moisture and cooler air aloft for a chance of\nshowers and isolated thunderstorms. The best chances will be\nSaturday afternoon as daytime heating destabilizes the \natmosphere. This is a much weaker storm than what we have just \nseen with precipitation amounts ranging from a trace to 0.20 \ninches. The low slowly heads eastward on Sunday with a stabilizing\nlayer of warmer air aloft moving in over much of the area.\nHowever, at least slight chances will continue over the Four \nCorners and along the Utah border over the higher terrain.\n\nFrom Monday into Thursday...Models are showing a fair and dry\nsouthwest flow developing over the area. Look for a bit warmer \ntemperatures and generally light winds. Expect some cloud \nincrease late in the period in advance of another Pacific low.\n\nNext Friday...Another low pressure system headed for our area? \nForecast models think that's a possibility. Something to keep an \neye on as we head through next week.",
